content: >-  
  ## Project Overview  
  This project analyzes student performance data containing names, ages, genders, and scores in Math, English, and Science.  
  The goal was to clean missing values, perform exploratory data analysis (EDA), and create an interactive Tableau dashboard for visualization.  
  👉 [**View the full notebook on Colab**](https://colab.research.google.com/drive/1lswrS9JlDFCfLtovM2RSyRbRUoCAMRI9?usp=sharing)  

  ---  

  ## Objectives  
  - Handle missing values using Python (mean for numeric fields, mode for categorical).  
  - Perform exploratory data analysis to understand distributions and relationships.  
  - Create visualizations (histograms, boxplots, averages) in Tableau to compare performance by gender.  
  - Build an interactive Tableau dashboard with filters for Gender and Age.  

  ---  

  ## Tools & Techniques  
  - **Python (pandas, numpy)** for data cleaning and preparation.  
  - **Matplotlib / Seaborn** for quick in-notebook visualization.  
  - **Tableau** for interactive data visualization and dashboard creation.  
  - Focused on handling missing data, comparing averages, and building clear visuals.  

  ---  

  ## Tableau Dashboard Components  
  - **Histograms:** Score distributions for Math, English, and Science.  
  - **Boxplots:** Score spread by Gender for each subject.  
  - **Average Lines:** Mean scores displayed per subject and gender.  
  - **Dashboard Filters:** Interactive Gender and Age filters for dynamic exploration.  
  - **Cards:** Filter cards, highlight cards, and optional parameter card for subject selection.  

  ---  

  ## Key Insights  
  - Average performance varied slightly by gender, with consistent median scores across subjects.  
  - The spread of Science scores was wider, indicating greater variability among students.  
  - The dashboard allows easy identification of outliers and score distributions by demographic group.  

  ---  

  ## Reflection & Next Steps  
  This project strengthened my understanding of EDA and Tableau dashboard design.  
  Next, I plan to:  
  - Add additional dimensions such as study hours or attendance if available.  
  - Automate the pipeline to refresh Tableau dashboards from updated datasets.  
  - Experiment with trend analysis over time in future versions.  

  ---  

  **Driven by data, defined by impact.**

